  "summary": "A personal Vinyl Record Collection Tracker. Each record has Title, Artist, Genre (Jazz/Rock/Classical dropdown), Estimated value (numeric EUR), and Status (defaults to Wishlist). Users can add, edit, delete records; acquire (Wishlist->Owned) and move to wishlist (Owned->Wishlist); filter by All/Wishlist/Owned; and see the summed Owned collection value in EUR. All data persists to localStorage and survives refreshes, with input validation and recovery from malformed stored data.",
  "implemented_features": [
    "Add a record with Title, Artist, Genre (dropdown), Estimated value (numeric); default status Wishlist",
    "Edit an existing record and reflect changes in the list",
    "Cancel an edit without persisting changes",
    "Delete a record",
    "Acquire flips a record from Wishlist to Owned (no-op on Owned)",
    "Move to wishlist flips an Owned record back to Wishlist (no-op on Wishlist)",
    "Validate input (required title/artist, valid genre, non-negative numeric value) with accessible per-field errors",
    "Filter the collection by All, Wishlist, or Owned",
    "Show summed Owned collection value in EUR with a live summary",
    "Persist records across browser refresh via localStorage",
    "Recover gracefully from malformed persisted data and deduplicate records by id",
    "Responsive, accessible UI with empty states and semantic controls"
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The idea lists Wishlist and Owned as Status values and that Status defaults to Wishlist; 'Acquire' and 'Move to wishlist' are the only status transitions, so the status is a two-state toggle rather than a free-text field. No other statuses were invented.",
    "The idea does not mandate confirmation dialogs for delete; the delete action is immediate to keep the journey minimal. Added no extra delete-confirmation requirement.",
    "Estimated value currency is EUR per the requirement; the value is stored as a number and displayed with EUR formatting. No currency conversion or multi-currency support was added since the idea scopes it to EUR.",
    "Filtering is limited to Wishlist (and All/Owned) as the idea specifies filtering to Wishlist; an 'All' view and an 'Owned' view were added so the filter is meaningful and reversible, consistent with the listed Status values.",
    "Persistence uses browser localStorage (single-user, no backend implied by the idea). Persistence is isolated behind a repository boundary so another client could replace it without UI changes.",
    "The idea does not request search/sort/export, so those features were omitted to keep the app minimal.",
    "Domain type named Vinyl (instead of Record) to avoid colliding with TypeScript's built-in Record<K,V> utility type; the user-facing label remains 'Record'."
  ],
